Feature: Handling
  The plain T1-S has no flight controller: only a receiver and two ESCs. The sticks move the
  ailerons, the elevator and the rudder directly, and nothing helps you. The plane flies as
  the real plane does. The top line of the HUD says MANUAL. L changes between high and low
  [[rates]]. X turns [[differential thrust]] on and off. The top line of the HUD shows both,
  for example "MANUAL | high rates | diff thrust on". The sim starts with high rates and
  differential thrust on.

  Expectation: Without a flight controller there is only one mode
    Self-levelling and rate hold are jobs for a flight controller, and the plain T1-S does
    not have one. M does nothing, and the plane stays in MANUAL.
    Given the flight controller is missing
    And the flight mode is MANUAL
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is MANUAL

  Expectation: Low rates for gentle flying
    The control surfaces move less for the same movement of the stick, so the plane turns
    more gently. Use low rates for smooth flight and for a landing.
    Given the rates are high
    When the pilot changes rates
    Then the rates are low

  Expectation: High rates for tight turns
    The control surfaces move through their full range. Use high rates for tight turns and
    rolls.
    Given the rates are low
    When the pilot changes rates
    Then the rates are high

  Expectation: Differential thrust off
    Only the rudder turns the plane in yaw, as on a plane with one motor.
    Given differential thrust is on
    When the pilot toggles differential thrust
    Then differential thrust is off

  Expectation: Differential thrust on
    The motors help the rudder. The outer motor turns faster and the inner motor turns more
    slowly, so the plane turns more quickly in yaw.
    Given differential thrust is off
    When the pilot toggles differential thrust
    Then differential thrust is on
